    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="pm_d57">

                <pb facs="pm_d57-1" n="1" xml:id="pm_d57-1"/>

                <head>PM–57. Telegram from the Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        Panama<anchor n="1" xml:id="pm_d57-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1960-09-15T16:40:00-04:00">September 15,
                            1960, 4:40 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>133. Eyes Only Ambassador.</p>
                <p>The President has determined that the Panamanian flag will be flown together with
                    the U.S. flag on a daily basis in Shaler’s Triangle, this action to be initiated
                    as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>If you see no overriding objection to following schedule, Dept suggests: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>At 9:00 a.m. EDT/ Sept 17th you will deliver to the Panamanian Foreign
                            Office the note quoted in Part 1 of Deptel 134<anchor n="2" xml:id="pm_d57-f2"/> and the Dept
                            will <pb facs="1072" n="984" type="typeset" xml:id="pg984"/> at the same
                            hour deliver to the Panamanian Embassy in Washington the note quoted in
                            Part 2 of Deptel 134.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>At 11:00 a.m. EDT/ September 17th you will issue the statement quoted
                            in Part 3 of Deptel 134.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>FYI/ Concurrently, the White House will issue parallel statement, text
                            of which will be cabled for your info when available.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>FYI / As soon thereafter as
                            physically possible, i.e., as soon as flag poles can be erected and
                            Shaler’s Triangle suitably neatened, hopefully following day but
                            certainly before October 1st, the flags will be flown.</item>
                        <pb facs="pm_d57-2" n="2" type="facsimile" xml:id="pm_d57-2"/>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>FYI. The flags will be raised and
                            lowered by U.S. personnel only.</item>
                        <label>6.</label>
                        <item>FYI. The modest costs incurred for
                            flag poles, etc., will be met through special funds. A clarifying
                            message on this will follow shortly. END FYI</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Re 4, 5 and 6, Dept Army instructed Governor of Canal Zone by separate
                        message.<anchor n="3" xml:id="pm_d57-f3"/></p>
                <p>In absence serious objection your part, in which case cable NIACT, you are instructed immediately to inform
                    the Governor of your instructions. You should also inform CINCARIB, stressing to both necessity holding
                    in confidence till public announcement. You may inform them these instructions
                    have White House concurrence.</p>
                <p>Please comment urgently on the drafts sent in DEPTEL 134.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Dillon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
